            "locator": "identityBranches within selected program scope",
            "excerpt": "## AMTOPP Scholarship\n\nEmployees of member companies qualify for applying for the Scholarship.\n\nComplete the application and return it to the AMTOPP office by January 5. It can be emailed or if mailed postmarked by January 5.\n\nAll the applications received will go into a drawing that will be held the last day of the annual conference, (Friday).\n\nNo late applications will be received, all must be in by or postmarked January 5.\n\n[provider contact sentence omitted]\n\n[Apply Now\\\\\n\\\\\n(opens in a new tab)](https://amtopp.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/AMTOPP-Member-Scholarship.pdf)\n\n[image omitted]\n\n## Future Farmers of America (FFA)\n\n[Apply Now\\\\\n\\\\\n(opens in a new tab)](https://montanaffa.org/applications/)\n\n- This program is open to seniors graduating from high schools in Montana and graduates of those high schools who are enrolled as freshmen at a college or vocational school in any state and planning to major in a field related to the horticultural or arboriculture  industry.\n- Applicants must be members of FFA and have completed at least 2 years of agricultural education classes.\n- They must have a GPA of 2.0 or higher.\n- Selection is based on academic achievement (10 points); FFA leadership, including agricultural education courses completed (15 points); an essay describing their career objectives and why they have selected a career or vocation in agriculture (15 points); their FFA Supervised Agricultural Experience (SAE) project (20 points); an essay on their community service and their role in those activities (10 points); financial need (5 points); a letter of reference from their adviser (5 points), and a letter of reference from a community member (5 points).\n\n[image omitted]\n\n"
